Just wanted to post the solution to this here... http://askubuntu.com/questions/687423/use-crontab-to-restart-an-upstart-service-on-schedule

Figured I'd leave this up here in case anybody else faces a similar problem in the future. Basically, just edit your root user's crontab to call /usr/sbin/restart shiny-server and you're good to go.

