Update:

Instead of changing the Repository field to "BioConductor", I removed it altogether.

newpackage$DESCRIPTION <- newpackage$DESCRIPTION[which(newpackage$DESCRIPTION!="")]

I managed to build my app correctly and deploy it to Shinyapps (yes!), but now I'm getting this error when I open my shiny app.

ERROR: /tmp/RtmpU3Ll2Q/file1a345c6196:50:1: unexpected input
49:                       KeyValueName="Value",...){
50: <c2>

I don't expect a fix for this issue soon. I'm not sure if its a problem with ComplexHeatmap, or Shinyapps, but for me, I think its time to throw in the towel on this one.

