Oh, oh, oh. This *totally* makes sense then--no bug in Shiny. Sorry, it didn't compute in my head when I looked at it. The problem is this:

runApp(list(server=server, ui=includeHTML(system.file('www', 'index.html', package='PanVizGenerator'))), ...)

The ui argument is assumed to be the main body of your UI, not an entire, complete HTML page. So of course we throw in our own shiny.js and jquery.js references. It totally makes sense.

So your "workaround" is absolutely the correct fix.

