MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I don't think this is shiny behaviour, I think the way file inputs in HTML work is that they only fire when they get a new file chosen. Re-choosing the file if it's the currently chosen file will not do anything. I think you have to manually choose a different file, and then again choose the original file.  Does that make sense?  I'm not 100% sure, but I think that's how file inputs work from what I remember

